[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: The inherited Version.format transition fails with AttributeError: SemverSolverSUT has no attribute 'format' raised from SemverSolverSUT.__getattr__ (line 241), because the implementation SUT aggregates only VersionEngine, PackageRepository, and DependencySolver and therefore cannot dispatch the contracted Version.format operation mandated by low/semver_solver.pyi, which requires format() to return the canonical SemVer string representation. Counterexample: SemverSolverFuzzTest rule_method(data=data(...)) selects the format transition, whose pivot must produce the canonical rendered string and assert ret equals it; instead the pivot raises AttributeError during attribute resolution on the SUT, so the postcondition is never verified and the contracted Version.format behavior is unreachable. Fix the pseudo-state machine by overriding the Version.format transition to invoke the concrete Version record's format method on the current model version (or by exposing a Version-typed member/service with a real format method in the SUT) so the rendered canonical string is returned and compared exactly, rather than leaving the pivot to fail attribute lookup.
